              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nothing new in this chapter. Not one word. Say the three forms you already have, in any order they come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the table you have earned",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three chapters, one form each. Now — and only now — they are worth seeing together:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "who",
                "ending, on hablar",
                "meaning"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "who: I. ending, on hablar: -o: hablo. meaning: I speak.",
                "who: tú. ending, on hablar: -as: hablas. meaning: you speak (a friend).",
                "who: él, ella, usted. ending, on hablar: -a: habla. meaning: he/she speaks, you speak (polite)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A table like this one at the start would have been three things at once and you would have memorised it. Arriving here, it is a picture of something you can already do."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the whole engine. Every regular -ar verb in Spanish — and there are thousands — runs on these three endings. You have not learned one verb. You have learned the pattern that fits all of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say what you do — hablo."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ask or state what a friend does — hablas."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say what someone else does, or address someone politely — habla."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do all three without a pronoun, because the ending carries it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all three in order — \"hablo, hablas, habla\"",
